    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting a massive 80.98 efficiency score, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite matchup against Merrill Kelly, whose 5.27 xERA is the softest target in our projected rotation. With the added weight on stolen base potential in our league format, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s profile is maximized by his leadoff spot and a favorable platoon advantage. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (74.02) provides substantial upside from the #3 hole; despite facing a lefty in Framber Valdez, the combination of favorable park factors and the +5% wind contribution pushes him well into \"Strong\" start territory, offering us the power-speed balance we prioritize.\n\nConversely, our benching of **Dillon Dingler** (37.62) highlights the strict discipline of the Zebras' roster construction. While **Dillon Dingler** hovered near our 40-point floor, his -15% dynamic platoon penalty against the right-handed Rasmussen\u2014combined with the inherent difficulty of facing a 3.26 xERA arm\u2014made him an easy exclusion for our efficiency-driven model. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Lars Nootbaar**. Should these lineup assumptions shift, particularly for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** against the formidable Logan Gilbert (3.46 xERA), we may see their scores fluctuate as the \"Order\" modifiers adjust to official batting slots. We are banking on **Lars Nootbaar** (58.28) to provide stable production against Kevin Gausman, as his +11% dynamic platoon edge narrowly offsets the danger posed by the opposing starter.",
